    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1890 the railroad had shifted the community’s focus, and Crawford boasted steam flour and corn mills, a cotton gin, and four churches.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/crawford-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town incorporated on August 12, 1897, marking its formal start as a municipality in western McLennan County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crawford%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Crawford is best known as the home of the 43rd U.S. president, George W. Bush, who spends part of his time at the nearby Prairie Chapel Ranch.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
